--TEST--
`Core\Config::secret` returns a `?secret string`, so `echo` and a plain `string` variable refuse it, its name cannot come from the request, and the values of an array setting convert to `tainted` text —`rule:config/settings-and-secrets-are-a-programs-own-values`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// A secret from `[secrets]` cannot be printed.
echo Core\Config::secret('api_key') ?? 'none';
string $key = Core\Config::secret('api_key') ?? '';

// The name of a secret cannot come from the request.
echo Core\Config::secret(Core\Request::query('name') ?? '') == null ? 'none' : 'set';

// The values of an array setting can be anything, so they are tainted.
array<string> $sizes = Core\Config::setting('sizes') as array<string>;

// A setting is not secret, so it can be printed.
echo Core\Config::setting('title') as ?string ?? 'none';
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0790]: `echo` cannot print a `secret` value
  --> case.nvs:3:6
%A
error[E0401]: expected `string`, found `string|secret string`
  --> case.nvs:4:15
%A
error[E0401]: expected `string`, found `string|tainted string`
  --> case.nvs:7:26
%A
error[E0401]: expected `array<string>`, found `array<tainted string>`
   --> case.nvs:10:24
%A
error: aborting due to 4 errors
%A
